WEBVTT

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.650
<b>25th 
Kitahidori Academy</b>

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.650
<b>Founding Festival</b>

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.780
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.790
Did you think it was just shumai?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.830
Today we've got pork buns, too!

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.290
I have Koyori waiting outside.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:32.230
We have data on how far apart you can get,

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.050
so we can talk with her out 
of the room for a little.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.010
<b>Yummy Curry</b>

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.010
<b>Yummy Home Curry</b>

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.840
I'm really sorry I never 
thought about a cell phone.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.270
<b>I'm Makihara</b>

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.270
It looks I've got a bad habit of 
only thinking about the future.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.200
There's something I wanted to ask today.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.270
Um...

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:53.080
Makihara-sensei, were you a Hand Shaker?

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.010
I didn't mean to hide it.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.420
That's right.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.860
I was once a Hand Shaker.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.450
But I never got to meet God.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.800
I lost the person whose hand 
I was supposed to hold.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.450
Oh, they're not dead!

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.990
Um, well...

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.810
A lot of stuff happened.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:29.310
Why did you put Koyori to sleep?

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.250
And why me...?

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.820
Koyori-kun

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.670
was born that way.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:42.750
She lost her memories and the 
ability to speak later though.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.950
It's not because she was always asleep?

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.890
But it's true...

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:49.870
I see.

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:51.940
I should've told you that, too.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:55.840
I don't know the precise cause either.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:01.320
But she was born a Hand Shaker,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.350
and there was once someone 
whose hand she held.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.350
Who was that?

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.290
I don't even know where they are now.

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:13.980
But if she loses the Hand Shaker 
whose hand she's supposed to hold,

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.610
Koyori-kun will disappear.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.610
So...

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.210
That's why I did that to her.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:27.130
All I could do was put her 
to sleep and keep her alive.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:29.620
So...

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:35.630
The fact that you were able to hold 
Koyori-kun's hand made me very happy.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:40.250
What I want to do and what I should 
do are meshing. That's all.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.390
I understand. I'll be going then.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:51.780
The school's busy with the 
school festival, right?

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.650
What about the shumai and the pork buns?

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.820
I'll just take this.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:03.910
All I've got to do at the festival 
is advertise and help in the store.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.660
It's nothing big.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.450
Bye.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.460
He knew about me...

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.700
Who told him?

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.180
I guess there are people out there...

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:25.160
My old friends and enemies.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.680
Sorry.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.060
You feeling okay?

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:34.190
This is from Makihara-sensei.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.560
You looked at mine a lot, too.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.160
You like looking, huh?

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.700
I thought you'd be here!

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.340
Tomoki!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.700
Trouble!

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.990
What is? You need something fixed?

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:53.820
No, President Lily!

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.840
You're friends, right?

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.960
Talk to her for me!

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.090
Now?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.490
<b>Student Council Room</b>

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.660
I love Masaru!

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.920
<b>Yummy Curry</b>

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.930
<b>25th 
Kitahidori Academy</b>

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.930
<b>Founding Festival</b>

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:08.930
Yes?

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.310
It's Takatsuki Tazuna.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:12.430
Can I come in?

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.330
Yes, please do.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:20.440
I'll go submit this paperwork.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.090
Okay, thanks.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.630
Welcome, Tazuna-kun.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:26.940
Hi...

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:28.940
What's wrong?

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:33.760
Um, someone from my class 
asked me to come here...

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.450
for something to do with the school festival.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.080
Yes.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.460
Is there anything I can do to help?

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:43.380
Um... President Lily, about what happened...

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.440
I have my own reason for fighting,

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.720
so I can't apologize, but...

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:55.690
No, I was the one who 
attacked without mercy...

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.980
Tazuna-kun, Koyori-chan...

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.420
We're the ones who did that.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.980
I ruined your... um... wish...

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.240
That's okay now.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.450
My wish is...

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.740
Um...

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.620
My parents are separating.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.980
Is that okay?

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:21.640
Do you want to talk about it?

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.460
No, that's not my wish!

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:28.600
It's sad, but...

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.470
Um...

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.930
Destruction. Ending.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:35.510
Reversed, it means a new beginning.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.120
It's certain that they're 
splitting up, and that's sad.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:40.090
But you know...

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:45.520
When I think that maybe they're able 
to be honest about their feelings now,

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.360
that makes me happy.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.850
And I...

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:55.360
I'm fine!

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.870
I'll talk about it some other time.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:00.630
Yeah.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:03.870
So what did you need, Tazuna-kun?

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:05.690
Well...

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.920
You can't get ingredients?

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.670
Yeah.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:14.540
We're having a little booth, right?

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:15.980
With light snacks.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:21.160
And Maeda said he could get 
us ingredients for cheap,

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.330
so we let him handle it.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:23.440
He was setting the prices, too.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:27.810
But his contact changed jobs a while ago...

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:30.030
So the whole plan fell apart?

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.280
That's why we're coming to you.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.300
You know President Lily, so can't you... um...

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.490
Do... something, you know?

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.580
That's crazy, and I don't 
know what "something" is.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:43.080
Please!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:46.650
I told the rest of the 
class to leave it to me!

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.790
I told them that!

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:52.800
I'm begging you, please!

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.670
No, but...

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.310
That is a problem, yes.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:57.300
There's less than a week to go.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:03.420
I know it's selfish, 
but I don't want our class to fail.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:07.520
I'm sorry.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.820
I was just thinking that 
that's just like you.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.320
When you see people in trouble,
 you repair things.

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:15.320
My hobbies are just meshing 
with what's good for everyone.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.340
Leave it to Student Council 
President Houjou Lily!

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:22.680
Can you come back tomorrow?

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.070
I'm sorry!

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:28.640
I'm sorry!

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:30.870
No, it's fine.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:34.990
I was so confident when I 
told you to leave it to me.

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:37.470
Masaru got really mad at me.

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.890
"You don't know anybody who 
can get you cheap food.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.780
Don't make offers like that!

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:45.190
Are you using your head?"

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:49.930
I was the one who asked 
for something so difficult.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:51.610
But he said that...

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:55.130
because he's worried about me, right?

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:57.860
Big sister can tell!

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.920
Connections, huh?

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:04.700
If we had something like that...

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:10.000
Masaru! You're so nice!

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:10.000
Oh? We do?

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.510
<b>Cocktail Corn</b>

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.510
I see.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:22.300
So you want to know if there's a way 
we can get you ingredients for cheap?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:23.760
That's it.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.990
I know it's selfish, but...

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:28.200
Sure.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:31.270
Really, Senpai? Just like that?

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.490
If we start now we can 
get them to you in time.

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:37.620
It's not like you need that much.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.020
It's good for us, too.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:43.140
So it's not a problem.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:44.730
If we can pull this off,

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:47.230
it'll help us sell your 
school that new cafeteria.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:49.730
And I can use that as a reason 
to give stuff to you cheap.

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:50.960
Jeez!

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.540
It's all part of a cunning plan, you see!

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:56.940
Sorry I'm not as smart as you.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:59.050
It's not that big a deal.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:01.150
Thanks.

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:02.300
That's a big help.

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:04.440
It's fine, really!

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:07.340
You and I are friends, after all.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:10.400
Why are you acting like 
you're the one who did it?

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:18.590
Senpai, you've got a 
wicked grin on your face.

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:21.070
I'm not thinking of anything bad.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:26.580
I'm just thinking I need to 
use this for something else!

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:31.580
<b>Cocktail Corn</b>

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:30.150
Tazuna-kun, sorry.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:37.590
<b>Takoyaki</b>

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:38.590
<b>Founding Festival</b>

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:41.090
<b>Standing Family Restaurant</b>

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:45.140
This is old.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:47.720
It's breaking in a lot of places.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.160
Will it last?

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:50.340
You really helped me!

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:53.770
You got the ingredients 
cheaper than planned.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.380
It means we've got lots of money left.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.520
I just happened to know someone.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:01.770
I didn't know I could count on you 
for things other than repairs.

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:04.890
Now I won't look like a liar.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:07.800
Takatsuki, thanks!

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.320
You know a lot of people, huh?

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:10.910
Thanks, Takatsuki-kun!

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.550
No, um...

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:15.920
You've kinda changed.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.270
Is it thanks to Koyori-chan?

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:19.690
You're easier to talk to than before.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:20.360
Oh, no!

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.420
That's bad!

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.430
That's really bad!

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:25.870
The bad news is gone.

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:28.540
My friend, Takatsuki Tazuna, 
has taken care of it.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.020
No!

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:35.380
All the chefs broke their arms 
while practicing secretly!

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:38.940
What did they do?

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:42.490
So we've lost all the people 
who can cook in our class?

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.950
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.360
Going to the mountains 
to train was a mistake.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.450
The mountains?

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.880
Koyori... You can't mean...

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.490
Are you really going to do it?

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:29.300
What kind of cooking videos 
have you been watching?

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:34.080
<b>Standing Family Restaurant</b>

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.080
Huh? Akutagawa-san can cook?

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:36.780
It's not simple.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:39.070
Cooking is about... the heart.

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:40.840
You can't do it yourself!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:44.220
I guess we could let her try.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:46.170
If you can give us some time every day...

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.210
Fingers in when you hold it.

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:56.490
Fingers in when you hold it.

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:59.240
Don't push too hard on the blade.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:02.150
Does this have anything to do with cooking?

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:05.780
It's starting to look like real cooking!

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.560
This burnt stuff is the 
secret ingredient, right?

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:10.090
It's your first time, so it's okay!

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:15.280
This color is... avant-guard, huh?

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.280
It's your second time, so it's okay!

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:17.020
That's right!

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:17.020
That's right.

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:18.470
Good work!

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.600
Wow, it tastes like 
something at a restaurant!

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.880
Yay!

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:27.050
It's delicious!

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:29.800
Oh, honey.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.020
Wow!

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.020
This is good!

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.160
We can do this!

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.800
They're all main dishes!

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:44.270
I see.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.060
It tastes okay.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:49.980
But on the festival day, 
are you going to be fast enough?

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:52.090
We can just help her then!

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:53.030
I think we can do it!

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.710
Is anybody else free?

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:58.540
Even with broken arms, we can at least help.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:03.040
<b>Founding Festival</b>

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:13.050
<b>Festival Concert</b>

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:17.060
<b>Standing Family Restaurant</b>

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:19.510
Thank you!

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:22.060
We came to check on you.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:25.050
Sorry to bother you when you're busy.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.900
Look at you two!

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.070
I remember when I was an school.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:33.840
Huh? Tazuna, is this your 
little sister or something?

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.500
I am

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.480
an adult!

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.790
I look good in this suit, right?

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.880
There, there...

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:44.790
Anyway, this is for Koyori-chan.

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:49.840
I can borrow her for a minute, right?

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:51.550
Remember what I said?

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:05.050
Well, Tazuna-kun?

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:09.070
It's cute, non-flammable, 
and doesn't get stained!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:12.570
Centeotl's special Japanese 
clothes for cooking!

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.920
Yeah, she's cute.

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:17.930
Why are you saying that?

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:19.720
No, sorry...

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.770
It's too late for apologies!

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:22.970
I'm sorry!

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:24.510
I'm sorry!

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.860
I bet you'd look good in it, too!

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:30.840
Koyori.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:38.350
You look good in it.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:48.060
Cute couple, huh?

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:50.110
I'm jealous.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.350
Thanks.

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:10.570
We're really busy thanks to you.

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:12.150
People like the food, too.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:16.380
There are clearly people who 
came to see Koyori-chan, as well.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:19.460
Are you tired?

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:23.890
Okay, hang in there.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:26.880
Oh, no!

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:28.150
<b>Standing Family Restaurant</b>

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.150
The flame disappeared!

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.630
It's no good. I can't get it to light.

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:34.990
It's old,

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:37.660
so I was hoping something 
like this wouldn't happen.

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:40.840
Can I do some emergency repairs?

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:41.960
But...

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:44.010
you and Koyori-chan have to cook.

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:45.790
You can do it, right?

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:48.060
Get me a screwdriver.

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:53.210
Here.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.560
Okay, it's fixed!

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:13.980
They're meshing, huh?

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.320
Tazuna-kun, Koyori-chan!

00:18:18.850 --> 00:18:20.320
President Lily.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.530
And...

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:25.550
Hello.

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:26.960
I'm not going to apologize, but...

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:28.410
Neither will I.

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:31.960
No, not now.

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:35.370
It's embarrassing. Stop it.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.190
The Star.

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:38.970
Hope.

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:41.960
You're blushing, huh?

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:45.720
Koyori-chan, let's exchange contact info.

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.670
Okay, if there's anything 
I can help with, I will.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:58.320
The student council just called you, right?

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.490
Is there anything I can do?

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:04.240
I can't cook.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.720
Okay. Ask Tomoki over there.

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:09.500
We need more people for a lot of things.

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:13.260
Let's play Precious Memories again.

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:16.750
The result was a dead end, but...

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:20.450
Me, too!

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:21.060
You get going, Sis.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.260
Masaru!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:30.060
Okay, thank you.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.260
We've still got plenty more!

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:42.240
It was a busy two days, huh?

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:46.070
Was it fun?

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:49.450
Me, too, I guess.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.230
It meshed, somehow.

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:53.580
Hey, good work.

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:59.590
I heard your class won the 
prize for best booth, huh?

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:04.940
Someone from my lab was 
talking about you, Koyori-kun.

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:07.290
They said there was a cute 
girl in Japanese clothes.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:09.850
That was Chizuru-san's idea.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:13.240
Tazuna-kun, thank you, really.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:17.860
Okay, don't stay out late.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:20.940
I'm busy, so I'll be going.

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:22.860
Um...

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:26.970
What's wrong?

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:28.760
Koyori?

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:35.300
You made this?

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:40.380
They're all main dishes!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:42.730
Let's eat!

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.320
Did it go well?

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:48.390
Just fine.

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:50.380
Hey, Rei-kun, there's a concert!

00:20:50.380 --> 00:20:51.640
Yeah, that looks good.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:52.570
Let's take a look.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.960
She looked good, huh?

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:02.490
Right? Good job, me!

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:05.930
Masaru.

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:13.030
<i>The diva stands on a bridge.</i>

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:16.730
<i>With sharp strikes that 
belie her cute exterior,</i>

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:18.680
<i>she praises Single Gear.</i>

00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:21.420
<i>The man who guides her dreams</i>

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:24.050
<i>is a producer who seems at 
first glance to be a clown.</i>

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:25.800
<i>He jokes around as he pushes them hard,</i>

00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:29.480
<i>and Tazuna and Koyori are 
terrified of their melody.</i>

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:34.740
<i>Next time on Hand Shakers,
Episode 8: Sing A Sonic.</i>

00:23:35.240 --> 00:23:36.670
Let it resound within you!

00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:38.490
Carve it into your soul!
